      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HERE COMES HOGAN (3) kept fresh and now in the Melissa Harrison yard. Tackled city class when eighth at Morphettville Parks over 1000m on the heavy (8) surface. Faces a far less daunting assignment this time with the claim. Leading contender. NORTHERN BOOGIE (1) proved too strong two runs ago at this track. Safely held last time out from the wide gate when eleventh over 1200m at Tamworth. Finds an easier assignment and can get the job done. MIDNIGHT RABBLE (4) turned things around last start and got the job done by a nose as public elect over 1000m at Wean. It doesn't get any easier but on his best form he is one of the chief contenders. BOLD TEE (7) hasn't been able to break through for an extended period. Ran twelfth over 950m at Cowra after he got a long way back in the run. Suitably placed so anticipating a bold performance.",
